* text=auto
*.ipynb filter=nbstripout
*.ipynb diff=ipynb

# PX 2013 and the PC-Axis support files that accompany it are CRLF formats: the
# production reference database is CRLF throughout, and so is every fixture checked in
# here. `* text=auto`
# stores them LF-normalised and then hands the working tree whatever the platform
# prefers - CRLF on Windows, LF on Linux. Since the engine now writes CRLF on every
# platform (from_pxmetadata_file.write_output, helpers/support_files.py), a Linux
# checkout would byte-compare fresh CRLF output against an LF fixture and fail a test
# that has nothing wrong with it. eol=crlf pins the working-tree form everywhere and
# rewrites no stored blob. NOT `-text`: that would freeze today's LF blobs into the
# Windows working tree too, and would only be correct together with renormalising all
# tracked .px/.vs/.agg files (85 at the time of writing, none containing NUL) to CRLF.
*.px eol=crlf
*.vs eol=crlf
*.agg eol=crlf
